Dad: Sira.
Dad: Where have you been?
Sira: ...
Dad: Don't you have things to do for today?
Dad: You haven't even helped the farmers tend their fields yet.
Sira: What was the Manajah Antang's result, dad?
Dad: Go ask the Balian.
Sira: And what if I already did? You're not gonna tell me yourself?
Dad: I have no time to talk to you.
Dad: Stop bothering me and go back to work.